✨ Montessori Math Adventure ✨

A fun, colourful, and interactive math game designed to help children build confidence in early numeracy skills through play.

Features include:
🍎 Counting Objects
🔢 Number Matching
➕ Addition
➖ Subtraction
📿 Place Value with Beads
✏️ Number Tracing
🏆 Rewards and Achievement System

The game is designed to make learning mathematics enjoyable while supporting Montessori-inspired learning principles.

💡 Ideal for preschool and early primary school children.

🚀 NEW: Math Strategies Adventure (Year 2 – Year 3)
https://mdabashar.github.io/Simple-Games/math-strategies-year3.html

For older children who are ready for bigger numbers and mental strategies:
➕ Addition: Jump, Split, Vertical (column), Make a ten, Round and adjust, Near doubles
➖ Subtraction: Jump back, Split (with renaming), Vertical (with trading), Count up, Round and adjust, Jump back through ten
✖️ Multiplication: Equal groups, Arrays, Skip counting, Doubling, Split (area model), Vertical
➗ Division: Sharing, Jump back (repeated subtraction), Think multiplication, Halving, Split, Remainders
📖 Learn mode with step-by-step worked examples and pictures (number lines, split trees, arrays, area models, column layouts)
✏️ Practice mode: "Step by step" (guided) or "On my own", with hints and the full working shown when needed
🎲 Mixed quiz · ⚡ Times tables · 📖 Story problems · 🖨️ Printable worksheets with answer key
🏆 Progress page with badges, a times-table map and a parents' corner showing which strategies need practice
Three levels: Year 2 review · Year 3 · Year 3 challenge

The original game is unchanged and now has a "🚀 Year 2–3 Maths" button on its menu.
Both games are also linked from https://mdabashar.github.io/Simple-Games/

Maisha Muneeba designed the game idea and learning concepts.

🎮 Try it here:
https://mdabashar.github.io/Simple-Games/montessori-math-v3-improved-fixed.html

She would love to hear your feedback and suggestions for future improvements!

